id: pm-gh1485
title: "GH-1485: Bound history-index reader contention before authoritative appends"
description: "Evaluate and bound writer delay from exclusive history-event-index readers while preserving authoritative history, invalidation, fallback and late-fact visibility. The reported mixed reader/writer workload retained correctness but breached its 2000ms real-time delivery SLO in one traced run."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[4]: "area:history","area:locking",github-intake,performance
created_at: "2026-10-16T13:01:36.615Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-18T00:49:28.626Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-18T00:49:27.470Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-18T00:49:27.470Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "Reproduce with isolated traced and untraced cohorts and report writer lock wait separately from downstream detection; Choose and document a bounded snapshot/fair-lock/critical-section protocol from measured attribution; Preserve authoritative fallback, committed invalidation and late-fact visibility; Prove zero lost or duplicate events, zero history drift and the declared end-to-end latency budget under mixed SDK and CLI writers."
goal: project management = context management
objective: Measure reader-versus-writer lock attribution and implement a bounded history-index read/write protocol without losing committed facts.
value: UI and agent watchers can observe project context without delaying authoritative mutations beyond a measured collaboration budget.
why_now: GH-1485 reports a 2247.5ms pre-append delay with at least 2071.0ms waiting for the history-index lock under 100 readers and ten writer lanes.
parent: pm-lvyd
risk: high
confidence: medium
severity: medium
resolution: "Read rows and size receipts coherently, close SQLite before asynchronous validation, and observe append-owner progress without taking writer locks. Preserve native contention evidence, fail fast for active projection contention and use portable invalidation. Bound repeated failed repairs with a shared five-second cooldown and recover after quiet intervals; retain stale-owner semantics and compatible cursors."
expected_result: Keep complete facts and bounded fixed-boundary delivery without projection writer queues or repeated full repair on every read.
actual_result: "Linked82 history/workflow and67 schema tests pass;467 focused tests exercise every history-index statement/function/branch. All four typechecks and41 final integration tests pass. Traced/untraced100-reader cohorts preserve5000 observations at1085/877ms below2000ms, with full index recovery after5500ms quiet. SDK import-cost checks and static prefix pass; qualified local CLI floor failures remain recorded with a paired-main comparison, while graph/record/mutation tail passes. Required live observability passes. Final-head complete hosted static/coverage/analyzers must pass before merge; no budget was relaxed."
component: history event index concurrency
