body: "Source: [GitHub issue 1485](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1485).\n\nThe report links the public pm-web capacity harness and unbraind/pm-web issue211. It separates traced and untraced runs, pre-append delay, index-lock wait lower bounds, downstream SDK classification, polling and SSE delivery. Preserve these distinctions and do not infer universal starvation from a perturbed run.\n\nImplementation and validation are recorded in the resolution, immutable close events and subsequent review history. The delivery replaces reader writer-lock sections with validated snapshots, preserves authoritative writer progress and bounds automatic repair retries after busy periods. Current ownership and lifecycle state are authoritative in the status and claim fields; the original intake-only scope no longer describes this delivery."
